+## Known gaps between the statements and the claims
+
+A 2026-10 source review of this pin (recorded in the parent integration
+repository, findings SM01–SM09 and SMT01–SMT07) found the following
+statement/claim gaps. They are open work, not proved results, and nothing
+above should be read as closing them:
+
+- The typed `flatScheme` in `Zkpc/Core/Flat.lean` is a typing exercise; no
+  refinement proof connects its algorithm bodies to `Core.Step`, and its
+  `spend`/`redeem` do not update the ledger records `sweep`/`dispute` read
+  (SM01).
+- `T5_payer_close_liveness` proves that *some* reachable settled state
+  exists, not that every fair execution settles by the deadline (SM02).
+- Refund `Step.forceClose` is enabled from every open state and forfeits
+  the whole deposit with no response window or proven-cheater guard, so the
+  refund layer is settlement arithmetic, not a proof of honest-payer
+  protection (SM03).
+- `flatInstance` resamples the epoch pseudonym on every emission (a real
+  epoch oracle repeats it within an epoch) and does not exclude digest `0`,
+  so it is not a checked ROM marginal of the stated ticket distribution;
+  the concrete-to-ideal view reduction is open (SM04).
+- T7 is the conditional blind-guess bound under `hobliv`, not the proposed
+  full bound, and the proposed full bound omits the zero-digest event (SM05,
+  item 1 above).
+- The real-wire bridges (O1–O4, ZK, rerandomization) remain definitions and
+  worklist items (SM06, items 2–3 above).
+- The FRAME `aReuse` calibration places a signal at digest `0`, which reveals
+  `k` whatever the slope, so it does not isolate slope reuse; and the
+  `multTag` one-ticket-safety claim fails for adversarial genesis state
+  (SM07).
+- Fleet `Conflict` (equal index, distinct messages) is not digest
+  inequality; a wire-level bridge must condition on or charge digest
+  collisions (SM09).
+- The K1–K4 review records in `research_knowledge/` are historical, each
+  at its own revision and with its own method limits. Three K3 claims go
+  beyond the current source: that T5's settlement event "provably occurs"
+  at the deadline (the theorem is existential, SM02), that the `multTag`
+  leak needs two challenge tickets (one suffices with adversarial genesis
+  state, SM07), and its suggested full T7 query budget (it omits the
+  zero-digest event, SM05). K4 was a simulated outside review, not an
+  independent human cryptographer's endorsement.
+- `Spec.md` T3's and T7's anti-vacuity notes were narrowed (SMT05): T3's
+  emission-based floor does not detect fresh-index retries, and slope reuse
+  needs two observations at distinct nonzero digests to leak `k`. A Lean
+  calibration of that two-observation experiment (against fresh slopes) is
+  still to be written.
